linear mixed-effect model for each issue $q$$(\alpha_q)_{n} = \beta_0 +\beta \cdot lr_n + wave + u_{n} + \epsilon$, (preregistered hypothesis H7).

\begin{tabular}{lccc}
issue & $\beta_0$ (mean and SE) & $\beta$ (mean and SE) & $p(|\beta|>0)$ \\ \hline
climate concern & $0.43$ ($\pm 0.02$) & $-0.23$ ($\pm 0.03$) & $<0.001$ *** \\
gay marriage & $0.43$ ($\pm 0.02$) & $-0.29$ ($\pm 0.03$) & $<0.001$ *** \\
migrant rights & $0.37$ ($\pm 0.02$) & $-0.10$ ($\pm 0.03$) & $0.002$ ** \\
economic inequality & $0.34$ ($\pm 0.02$) & $-0.18$ ($\pm 0.03$) & $<0.001$ *** \\
digital regulation & $0.21$ ($\pm 0.02$) & $-0.02$ ($\pm 0.03$) & $0.389$  \\
East Germans' recognition & $0.22$ ($\pm 0.01$) & $-0.01$ ($\pm 0.03$) & $0.830$  \\
\end{tabular}

  climate concern              wave p=0.07 R2=0.03/0.57 converged=True
  gay marriage                 wave p=0.63 R2=0.05/0.53 converged=True
  migrant rights               wave p=0.20 R2=0.01/0.53 converged=True
  economic inequality          wave p=0.55 R2=0.02/0.47 converged=True
  digital regulation           wave p=0.58 R2=0.00/0.39 converged=True
  East Germans' recognition    wave p=0.15 R2=0.00/0.40 converged=True
joint model with interaction effects
\begin{equation}
    \alpha_{n,q} = \beta_0 + \beta_1 \, \mathrm{lr}_n + \sum_{q' \neq q_\mathrm{ref}} \beta_{q'} \, \mathbb{I}[q=q'] + \sum_{q' \neq q_\mathrm{ref}} \beta_{\mathrm{lr}\times q'} \, \mathrm{lr}_n \, \mathbb{I}[q=q'] + \beta_\mathrm{wave} \, \mathbb{I}[\mathrm{wave}=2] + u_n + \epsilon_{n,q},
\end{equation}
where $u_n \sim \mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_u^2)$ are participant-level random intercepts and $q_\mathrm{ref}$ is digital regulation. Hence $\beta_1$ is the slope of $\mathrm{lr}$ for $q_\mathrm{ref}$, and $\beta_1+\beta_{\mathrm{lr}\times q'}$ is the slope for issue $q'$. 
The fit parameters are (converged=True):\\
